WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.043
Google Cloud credentials and sessions are
sensitive operational authority.

2
00:00:09.123 --> 00:00:17.667
They may exist as local CLI login
sessions, Application Default Credentials,

3
00:00:17.747 --> 00:00:24.995
service account key files, token caches,
federated credentials,

4
00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:33.360
workload identity, metadata-based
credentials, environment variables,

5
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.970
CI/CD secret stores, or temporary files.

6
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:44.522
The presence of a credential defines what
the script can do,

7
00:00:44.602 --> 00:00:48.356
even if the script never prints it.

8
00:00:48.436 --> 00:00:57.886
Long-lived service account key files
should be minimized where better options exist.

9
00:00:57.966 --> 00:01:05.085
Workload Identity Federation, service
account impersonation,

10
00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:14.485
metadata-based runtime identity, and
short-lived credentials can reduce risk when

11
00:01:14.565 --> 00:01:17.413
they fit the environment.

12
00:01:17.493 --> 00:01:23.576
These approaches do not remove the need
for validation,

13
00:01:23.656 --> 00:01:32.200
but they reduce reliance on durable key
material that can be copied, retained,

14
00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.833
or misplaced.

15
00:01:33.913 --> 00:01:43.104
Scripts should check whether required
login context and credentials are available

16
00:01:43.184 --> 00:01:49.915
without printing tokens, key material, or
sensitive values.

17
00:01:49.995 --> 00:01:57.373
Avoid exposing credential-derived values
in logs, shell history,

18
00:01:57.453 --> 00:02:05.349
debug traces, artifacts, support bundles,
and full environment dumps.

19
00:02:05.429 --> 00:02:11.642
CI/CD masking can help, but it is not a
complete boundary;

20
00:02:11.722 --> 00:02:17.806
transformed values, temporary files,
verbose output,

21
00:02:17.886 --> 00:02:22.805
and artifacts can still leak sensitive
data.

22
00:02:22.885 --> 00:02:32.464
Credential handling includes rotation,
revocation, ownership, and lifetime limits.

23
00:02:32.544 --> 00:02:39.922
Teams should know how to disable a service
account key if one exists,

24
00:02:40.002 --> 00:02:48.416
revoke a session, review impersonation
access, pause a federated workflow,

25
00:02:48.496 --> 00:02:53.156
and identify which jobs used a credential.

26
00:02:53.236 --> 00:03:02.167
Secure Google Cloud CLI automation treats
credentials as scoped and reviewable,

27
00:03:02.247 --> 00:03:06.260
not permanent background plumbing.
